torch.no_grad() will ensure the gradients are not accumulated
last_hidden_state[:, 0, :]  contains [batch_sizes/chunks, tokens, hidden dimension]
tokens can [CLS], [SEP], [PAD] [CLS] contains the classification of the correesponding text and its meaning.

Using **inputs is the same as writing:
outputs = model(input_ids=inputs["input_ids"], attention_mask=inputs["attention_mask"])
** unpacks the dictionary into individual named arguments which contains input_ids and attention mask which will have 0 and 1. 0 for padding

chroma db stores data as lists format, it has ephimeral method to create client which restart a db each time, persistent method creates a db once and gets it each time.
it's client-server type method needs a server to run in and it supports multiple users to access at a time.

